course: dictionary
lesson: 14555
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right. Look at the capital letter first. «Phoebe kicked the ball over the fence.» Phoebe starts with a capital P and is doing something a person does, so it is a girl's name.
explain: Now look at the small letter and the clues around it. «A phoebe sat on the branch and wagged its tail.» A phoebe with a small p is a bird, because it sat on a branch and wagged its tail.
explain: Space words give clues too. «Phoebe is a small, dark moon of Saturn.» Moon and Saturn tell you this Phoebe is not a person or a bird. Always check: which meaning fits the sentence?
fact: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Phoebe is a girl's name. It comes from an old Greek word meaning bright or shining.
fact: A phoebe with a small p is a small grey-brown bird of North America. It catches flies in the air and wags its tail.
fact: Phoebe is also one of the moons of Saturn. It is small and dark, and it goes round the planet backwards.
fact: In Greek myths, Phoebe was a Titan, a goddess linked with the Moon and light.
exercise: «Phoebe put her bag by the door before school.» In this sentence, Phoebe is | *A girl's name | A goddess of the sea | A moon of Saturn | A small grey-brown bird
exercise: «A phoebe sat on the branch and wagged its tail.» What is a phoebe here? | A planet | A kind of flower | *A small bird | A girl at school
exercise: Which clue shows that Phoebe is a name and not a bird? | It catches flies | *The capital P at the start of the word | It is very small | It goes round a planet
test: «Phoebe is one of the moons of Saturn.» In this sentence, Phoebe means | A Titan from Greek myths | A girl's name | A bird that wags its tail | *A moon
test: The name Phoebe comes from an old Greek word. What does that word mean? | Dark and cold | A fast runner | *Bright or shining | A grey, wet day
exam: «The phoebe flew down to catch a fly in the air.» What is a phoebe in this sentence? | A moon of Saturn | *A small bird that catches flies | A girl with a capital P | A goddess who lives on the Moon
